# Enrichment tiers (smart — not every edit needs a full KG rebuild)

## Decision matrix

| What changed | Action | Command / artifact |
|--------------|--------|------------------|
| **Shipped code** in `novopay-*` / `trustt-*` (processor, orchestration XML, entity, batch) | **Tier FULL** — graph spine may have changed | `cursor-bundle/kg/bin/build.sh` or `scripts/bin/kg-switch.sh` after branch checkout |
| **Shipped fix** — brain changelog only (behaviour note, no new apiName in code) | **Tier CASES** — precedents from CHANGELOG | `cursor-bundle/kg/bin/changelog-add.sh` (auto) or `build.sh --cases-only` / `refresh_cases.py` |
| **KB only** — `.cursor/changelog.md`, `gaps-and-risks.md`, `accounting-module-knowledge.mdc`, demo scripts, `system_brain/` notes | **Tier SKIP** — no KG rebuild | Append/update docs only |
| **Repo branch/sha drift** or orchestration XML newer than `kg.db` | **Tier FULL** | `kg doctor` → `kg-switch.sh` |
| **Gap resolved / runbook** | **Tier SKIP** (unless new apiName or orchestration fact) | `gaps-and-risks.md` / `cursor-bundle/brain/runbooks/` |

**Rule of thumb:** If `kg flow <apiName>` would change → FULL. If only “we fixed X before” history → CASES. If humans-only narrative → SKIP.

## Shipped fix (same task turn, before push)

1. **Brain changelog** — prepend with **SHA + apiName + tables** in detail line:
   ```bash
   cursor-bundle/kg/bin/changelog-add.sh \
     "## YYYY-MM-DD | acct \`3966ffa3c\` | accounting-v2 | branch | title" \
     "fetchLoanForeclosureSimulationDetails billed_dpi=0: … loan_due_details …"
   ```
   Names `apiName` verbatim so `kg cases <apiName>` links the precedent.

2. **Agent KB** — append `.cursor/changelog.md` (one line).

3. **Gaps / runbook** — only when symptom class or gap status changes (SKIP KG).

`changelog-add.sh` runs **cases refresh** when watermark in sync; **full build** when code drift.

## Automation

| Trigger | Tier |
|---------|------|
| `git push` success | `enrichment-sync.sh` — FULL if watermark/orch drift; CASES if CHANGELOG newer only; else SKIP |
| `git commit` | `.pending-kg-rebuild` flag (reminder) |
| `git push` without brain CHANGELOG | blocked (`enrichment-audit.sh --pre-push`) |
| Session start / workspace open | `enrichment-sync.sh` + `workspace-kg-state.md` |
| `build.sh` cache hit + CHANGELOG newer | `refresh_cases.py` (not silent stale cases) |

## End-of-task output (mandatory)

```
Knowledge updated: [brain CHANGELOG | gaps | runbook | .cursor/changelog | none]
KG enrichment: [FULL | CASES — <reason> | SKIP — KB only]
KG cases: [<apiName> — N precedent(s) | n/a]
Changelog: [appended | n/a]
```

## Discuss-before-updating exception

Does **not** apply to enrichment when user asked to **ship/fix** code — brain CHANGELOG is part of shipping. KB-only doc edits never require KG unless they name new orchestration facts.
